{"timestamp":"2026-08-26T03:13:40.867Z","ordinal":19,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a03c0f-2603-70a1-8c97-bfc0b84b9398","call_id":"call_YDjxCUd83t1voSqJdDVypH4h","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Create ChatKit session | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/typescript/resources/beta/subresources/chatkit/subresources/sessions/methods/create)\nciteturn0search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; client.beta.chatkit.sessions.create(SessionCreateParams { user, workflow, chatkit_configuration, 2 more } body, RequestOptions options?): ChatSession { id, chatkit_configuration, client_secret, 7 more } ... chatkit_configuration?: ChatSessionChatKitConfigurationParam { automatic_thread_titling, file_upload, history } ...     `import OpenAI from 'openai';\n\n# Create ChatKit session\n\nclient.beta.chatkit.sessions.create(SessionCreateParams { user, workflow, chatkit_configuration, 2 more } body, RequestOptions options?): ChatSession { id, chatkit_configuration, client_secret, 7 more }\n\nPOST/chatkit/sessions\n\nCreate a ChatKit session.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\nbody: SessionCreateParams { user, workflow, chatkit_configuration, 2 more }\n\nuser: string\n\nA free-form string that identifies your end user; ensures this Session can access other objects that have the same `user` scope.\n\nminLength 1\n\nworkflow: ChatSessionWorkflowParam { id, state_variables, tracing, version }\n\nWorkflow that powers the session.\n\nView schema details\n\nchatkit_configuration?: ChatSessionChatKitConfigurationParam { automatic_thread_titling, file_upload, history }\n\nOptional overrides for ChatKit runtime configuration features\n\nView schema details\n\nexpires_after?: ChatSessionExpiresAfterParam { anchor, seconds }\n\nOptional override for session expiration timing in seconds from creation. Defaults to 10 minutes.\n\nView schema details\n\nrate_limits?: ChatSessionRateLimitsParam { max_requests_per_1_minute }\n\nOptional override for per-minute request limits. When omitted, defaults to 10.\n\nView schema details\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nChatSession { id, chatkit_configuration, client_secret, 7 more }\n\nRepresents a ChatKit session and its resolved configuration.\n\nid: string\n\nIdentifier for the ChatKit session.\n\nchatkit_configuration: ChatSessionChatKitConfiguration { automatic_thread_titling, file_upload, history }\n\nResolved ChatKit feature configuration for the session.\n\nView schema details\n\nclient_secret: string\n\nEphemeral client secret that authenticates session requests.\n\nexpires_at: number\n\nUnix timestamp (in seconds) for when the session expires.\n\nformat unixtime\n\nmax_requests_per_1_minute: number\n\nConvenience copy of the per-minute request limit.\n\nobject: \"chatkit.session\"\n\nType discriminator that is always `chatkit.session`.\n\nrate_limits: ChatSessionRateLimits { max_requests_per_1_minute }\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCreate a conversation | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/python/resources/conversations/methods/create)\nciteturn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; conversations.create(ConversationCreateParams**kwargs) -> Conversation ...     `from openai import OpenAI\n\n# Create a conversation\n\nconversations.create(ConversationCreateParams**kwargs) -> Conversation\n\nPOST/conversations\n\nCreate a conversation.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\nitems: Optional[Iterable[ResponseInputItemParam]]\n\nInitial items to include in the conversation context. You may add up to 20 items at a time.\n\nView schema details\n\nmetadata: Optional[Metadata]\n\nSet of 16 key-value pairs that can be attached to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format, and querying for objects via API or the dashboard.\n\nKeys are strings with a maximum length of 64 characters. Values are strings with a maximum length of 512 characters.\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nclass Conversation: …\n\nid: str\n\nThe unique ID of the conversation.\n\ncreated_at: int\n\nThe time at which the conversation was created, measured in seconds since the Unix epoch.\n\nformat unixtime\n\nmetadata: object\n\nSet of 16 key-value pairs that can be attached to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format, and querying for objects via API or the dashboard. Keys are strings with a maximum length of 64 characters. Values are strings with a maximum length of 512 characters.\n\nobject: Literal[\"conversation\"]\n\nThe object type, which is always `conversation`.\n\n### Create a conversation\n\nPython\n    \n    `from openai import OpenAI\n    client = OpenAI()\n    \n    conversation = client.conversations.create(\n      metadata={\"topic\": \"demo\"},\n      items=[\n        {\"type\": \"message\", \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"}\n      ]\n    )\n    print(conversation)\n    `\n    \n    `{\n      \"id\": \"conv_123\",\n      \"object\": \"conversation\",\n      \"created_at\": 1741900000,\n      \"metadata\": {\"topic\": \"demo\"}\n    }\n    `\n\n##### Returns Examples\n    \n    `{\n      \"id\": \"conv_123\",\n      \"object\": \"conversation\",\n      \"created_at\": 1741900000,\n      \"metadata\": {\"topic\": \"demo\"}\n    }\n    `--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommunity | OpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/community)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; See programs Share what you built Submit your project, demo, or workflow to the OpenAI developer showcase. ... Codex Ambassadors Host local workshops and meetups for developers in your city. ... > I started a session locally on codex app > had to leave so I handed it off to